==English==

===Etymology===
{{rfe|en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-all in all.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|modal|set phrase}} [[generally|Generally]], [[all things considered]]
#: '''''All in all''', it's not a bad little restaurant.''
# Altogether
#: ''There were twenty absentees '''all in all'''''.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|generally}} {{l|en|for the most part}}, {{l|en|mostly}}, {{l|en|on the whole}}, {{l|en|altogether}}, {{l|en|in all}}, ''[[summa summarum]]''; see also [[Thesaurus:mostly]]

